            "description": "Watch Rosario Central vs Libertad Asuncion highlights and goals from CONMEBOL Libertadores on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on May 5, 2026. The stands were pulsing with the unique energy of South American football as two continental powers faced off in pursuit of supremacy. The match promised to be a tactical battle of nerves, where every inch of the pitch would be contested with maximum intensity. Tense Opening and a Missed Opportunity On May 5, 2026 , Rosario Central and Libertad Asuncion met in the CONMEBOL Libertadores in a clash defined by physical rigor from the opening whistle. The referee was kept busy early on, distributing yellow cards to Gustavo Aguilar and Robert Rojas for the visitors, while Agustin Sandez was booked for the home side. The most dramatic moment of the first half arrived in the 43rd minute when a penalty was awarded to the hosts. The veteran Angel Di Maria stepped up to take the spot-kick, but to the shock of the home crowd, he failed to convert, leaving the game scoreless at the interval. Ovando Finds the Breakthrough The second half began with strategic changes, as Enzo Copetti and Rodrigo Villalba were introduced to provide fresh legs. Rosario Central 's persistence finally paid off in the 57th minute. Ignacio Ovando found space in the final third and clinicaly finished to put the Argentine side ahead. The goal shifted the momentum of the match, forcing Libertad to push forward, which led to further cautions for Gaston Avila and Federico Carrizo as the tactical battle intensified in the midfield. Defensive Resilience and Final Whistle In the closing stages, the home side turned to their bench to solidify the result, bringing on Carlos Quintana and Federico Navarro to shore up the defense. Libertad threw everything forward in search of an equalizer, with Jorge Recalde picking up a yellow card in stoppage time as frustrations mounted. Despite six minutes of added time and late pressure from the Paraguayan side, Rosario Central held firm to secure a crucial victory in their continental campaign.",
